        "id": 5030,
        "name": "Rabit",
        "username": "Rabit",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
        "created_at": "2011-08-08T20:28:02.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I had a thought earlier today and wanted to share: I’m <span class=\"bbcode-i\">really</span> glad Sentinels of the Multiverse is not a collectable card game. I think allowing us to enjoy the universe, creating interesting and impactful flavor while providing enough mechanics and capabilities to ensure many unique and enjoyable games was a much better way to go.</p>\n<p>It would have been easy to make the leap to a CCG as another money-making opportunity, but the fact that the game can be expanded just by expanding the multiverse will hopefully help keep you in business.</p>\n<p>And maybe one day we’ll even see actual comics.  8)</p>\n<p>Many thanks!  <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/smiley.png?v=9\" title=\":smiley:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":smiley:\"></p>\n<p>Rabit</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:34:34.848Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 1,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 5.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 5028,
        "topic_slug": "thanks-for-not-making-it-a-ccg",
