        "id": 20660,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2011-08-09T13:01:09.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I complete agree, it’s the one reason I was never able to get into Magic of the Gathering is because it would cost way too much money to actually get a good deck of cards that can actually do some damage on opposing players, money I surely don’t have. There is also the fact that Sentinels of the Multiverse is a cooperative game which doesn’t have any bad blood when someone beats another, since everyone either wins or loses together.</p>",
